# Local environment template
#
# Copy this to the agentic-os-template repo root as `local.env` and fill in machine-specific
# values. `local.env` is gitignored and must never be committed.
#
# install.sh reads this file. bootstrap.sh creates it.
#
# Co-located default (claude + codex): leave CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR / CODEX_HOME empty
# and bootstrap renders each harness's config into a gitignored dir under this
# repo (<repo>/.claude, <repo>/.codex) so a fresh clone runs self-contained. Set
# them (or run bootstrap with --scattered / -Scattered) to use your home dir
# instead. Hermes is the exception — see HERMES_HOME below.

# claude harness build target — the directory named by the CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR
# environment variable.
#   LEAVE EMPTY for the co-located default: bootstrap renders into <repo>/.claude
#   (gitignored). SET an absolute path (e.g. ~/.claude) to scatter config to your
#   home dir instead — or run bootstrap with --scattered / -Scattered. Quote it
#   if the path contains spaces — this file is sourced.
CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=

# codex harness build target — the directory named by the CODEX_HOME environment
# variable; Codex defaults it to ~/.codex.
#   LEAVE EMPTY for the co-located default: <repo>/.codex (gitignored). SET an
#   absolute path (e.g. ~/.codex) to scatter — or use --scattered / -Scattered.
#   bootstrap also exports the resolved value to your shell (~/.zshenv) / User
#   env so the codex CLI actually uses it. Quote it if the path contains spaces —
#   this file is sourced.
CODEX_HOME=

# REQUIRED for the hermes harness — absolute path to the Hermes home or profile
# dir (the build target for `install.sh --harness hermes`), named by the
# HERMES_HOME environment variable; Hermes defaults it to ~/.hermes, and a
# dedicated profile dir is the safe target (see harnesses/hermes/adapter.md).
#   NOT co-located by default (unlike claude/codex): ~/.hermes is a live
#   desktop-app home (databases, auth, a bundled runtime, native skills) that the
#   app discovers at its OWN default path, NOT via this variable — so pointing it
#   at a repo subdir would render the spine into a dir the GUI never reads. Leave
#   it at ~/.hermes (or your profile dir); --scattered does not affect it. Quote
#   it if the path contains spaces — this file is sourced.
HERMES_HOME=

# OPTIONAL — absolute path to this agentic-os-template checkout. Defaults to the
# repo root that install.sh / bootstrap compute from their own location. It is
# also the base for the co-located CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR / CODEX_HOME defaults
# (<AI_CONFIG_DIR>/.claude, <AI_CONFIG_DIR>/.codex); set it only to override.
AI_CONFIG_DIR=

# OPTIONAL (claude harness) — absolute path to a local SKILLS overlay file. The
# shipped harnesses/claude/SKILLS.template.md is spine-only; install.sh appends
# this file's contents at the operator-overlay marker when set, reproducing your
# full plugin/family/MCP/CLI catalog in the rendered SKILLS.md. Leave empty for a
# spine-only render (the framework default — friends cloning the template start
# here). The overlay file is operator-local and is never shipped — keep it at the
# repo root as local.skills-overlay.md (the shipped .gitignore covers that name,
# guarding against an accidental git add; a forced add still bypasses it). Quote
# it if the path contains spaces — this file is sourced.
SKILLS_OVERLAY_PATH=

# OPTIONAL (codex harness) — absolute path to a local codex-rules overlay file.
# The shipped harnesses/codex/AGENTS.template.md is spine-only; install.sh
# --harness codex appends this file's contents at the operator-overlay marker
# when set, reproducing any operator tool-policy rules in the rendered AGENTS.md.
# Codex (unlike the claude harness) has no auto-loaded rules/ sidecar dir, so
# these rules must land in AGENTS.md itself. Leave empty for a spine-only render
# (the framework default — friends cloning the template start here). The overlay
# file is operator-local and is never shipped — keep it at the repo root as
# local.codex-rules-overlay.md (the shipped .gitignore covers that name,
# guarding against an accidental git add; a forced add still bypasses it). Quote
# it if the path contains spaces — this file is sourced.
CODEX_RULES_OVERLAY_PATH=

# OPTIONAL (hermes harness) — absolute path to a local soul-identity file. The
# shipped harnesses/hermes/SOUL.template.md carries the framework operating
# section plus a single @@OPERATOR_SOUL_IDENTITY@@ marker; install.sh --harness
# hermes splices this file's contents at the marker, making the rendered SOUL.md
# identity-first (who the operator is + how to work with them — a lean projection
# of the durable vault Operator Soul note). Leave empty for an identity-less
# spine render (the framework default — friends cloning the template start here).
# The file is operator-local and is NEVER shipped — it carries personal identity
# and machine paths, so keep it at the repo root as local.soul-identity.md (the
# shipped .gitignore covers that name). Keep it plain prose: no `@@…@@`
# framework tokens (they are build-time substitution markers — a literal one in
# the identity would be stripped or expanded, not rendered verbatim). Quote the
# path if it contains spaces — this file is sourced.
SOUL_IDENTITY_PATH=

# OPTIONAL — operator identity tokens for the cleanliness guard
# (scripts/check-clean.{sh,ps1}): comma-separated personal name / handle /
# hostname tokens the guard scans tracked CONTENT for, case-insensitively.
# Unset, the structural scans still run; only the personal-token classes are
# skipped. Never committed — the shipped guard carries zero operator identity.
OPERATOR_PII_TOKENS=

# OPTIONAL — tracker issue-key prefix(es) for the cleanliness guard:
# comma-separated Linear-style team keys (e.g. ABC or ABC,OPS — a letter
# followed by letters/digits). check-clean derives its tracker-ID scan from
# these so any configured tracker's issue IDs are kept out of the public tree,
# not just the historical default. Unset, the guard scans for QUE (back-compat
# with existing CI fixtures). TEAM is RESERVED as the framework's documentation
# placeholder. Both placeholder shapes framework files carry — digitless TEAM-NN
# and bracketed <TEAM>-<digits> (the '>' breaks prefix-digit adjacency) — match
# no prefix scan, even a configured TEAM; keeping TEAM out of real configs
# preserves that guarantee for future prose, so use your actual team key.
TRACKER_ISSUE_PREFIX=

# OPTIONAL — commit-metadata identity allowlist for the cleanliness guard:
# comma-separated exact `Name <email>` entries. When set, check-clean FAILS any
# ahead-of-default branch commit whose author or committer is not on this list
# (content scans cannot see commit metadata — a clone with no repo-local git
# identity derives your personal name + machine hostname into public history).
# Unset, the check is a documented no-op. Quote the value — it contains spaces.
# Format limit: an identity whose NAME itself contains a comma cannot be
# expressed (the comma reads as a separator); the mismatch fails closed.
COMMIT_IDENTITY_ALLOWLIST=

# See obsidian/vault-guide.md §3 for vault setup walkthrough.
# OPTIONAL — absolute path to the durable-knowledge vault. install.sh substitutes
# this into the generated harness entrypoint (`CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, or
# `SOUL.md`, per the chosen --harness). Leave it EMPTY to start: the framework
# degrades gracefully — the entrypoint renders an "unset" note and the spine runs
# without durable-knowledge context. Set it (and re-run install) to wire the layer.
# Quote it if the path contains spaces — this file is sourced.
OBSIDIAN_VAULT_PATH=

# See linear/linear-setup.md §3 for Linear access surface setup
# (both lineark CLI and Linear MCP options). Optional — Linear access is
# operator-configured; the framework gracefully degrades when neither
# surface is installed.
LINEAR_WORKSPACE_URL=

# OPTIONAL — absolute path to the harness memory store the maintenance scans
# (check-memory-drift, check-distillation-completeness, self-audit) should
# treat as primary when several projects/*/memory stores exist. Unset, the
# scripts aggregate every store they discover; set it to pin one explicitly.
# Quote it if the path contains spaces — this file is sourced.
CLAUDE_PRIMARY_MEMORY_DIR=

# OPTIONAL — soft per-session injection budget for self-audit, in whole KB
# (default 32). Every kickoff orient injects MEMORY.md + the rendered CLAUDE.md
# + the vault START.md + the operator-identity note; past this budget self-audit
# WARNS — never blocks — so raise it here if a larger surface is deliberate.
INJECTION_SURFACE_WARN_KB=
